                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Apparently this game is now free haha. I looked it up and I bought this in 2015 for $9. Oh the joys of a massive backlog. Anyway this is a very point & click game. There are several puzzles in this that I don't think you could figure out (except maybe just trial and error?). Some are somewhat figureoutable but some....if there wasn't a walkthrough I wouldn't have finished it. Its very short, my 3 hour runtime is me folliwing a guide for most of it. (I did the first puzzle myself, immediately got stuck and then followed the steam guide). since it is pretty short, the characters feel kinda shallow and somehow this game moves very slow and very fast at the same time. \r\nI really do like that some of the puzzles require you to type out your answer, that is a cool and unique thing I haven't seen much. \r\nOverall this game is a product of its time. Its 11 years old. Is it scary? not terribly, but I still enjoyed it. Go in expecting obtuse point & click puzzles, very light horror and some silly moments and the possibility for a random 'intimate scene' as the guide calls it haha . (also as someone who loves Lovecraftian things, this really isn't.)\r\n",
